{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>לא ימשול למכרה בבגדו בה — he has no authority to sell her, having betrayed her.</b> Like מדוע נבגוד איש באחיו (Malachi 2:10). It is true and correct that the master has no authority to sell her to a man of Israel, and this we know from tradition. He [Scripture] placed this as a remembrance and as an asmakhta. Do not marvel because of 'to a foreign people' [לעם נכרי] in this verse, for it is like שלם ישלם (below, 22:2), as I shall explain. The Gaon [Saadia] said that לעם נכרי is like לאיש נכרי, and like it is הגוי גם צדיק תהרוג (Genesis 20:4). But this is impossible to say concerning an individual in any of the [grammatical] forms, for it is correct to say ויאמר ישראל since it is a collective species-name, like ויאמר מצרים (above, 14:25). Only because it is a word whose meaning is collective — like עם, גוי, קהל, עדה — it is impossible to say of an individual. And the meaning of הגוי גם צדיק is an explicit noun, for 'you have brought upon me and upon my kingdom a great sin' (Genesis 20:9)." "<b>וטעם לא תצא כצאת העבדים — and the sense of 'she shall not go out as the slaves go out.'</b> Their going out is always after six years, for this one too shall go out if six years have arrived, as it is written: כי ימכר לך אחיך העברי או העבריה ועבדך שש שנים (Deuteronomy 15:12). Only if she arrived [at the time of her release] before six, at the time when she is in her own authority, she shall go out." "<b>אם רעה — if evil.</b> That she did not find favor in his eyes after he acquired her, to take her as a wife. And this is the sense of אשר לו יעדה — that she was designated for him to be his wife, or he designated her to be his son's wife. And know that לו is the qeri, and the ketiv is with alef: לא. The Gaon [Saadia] said that [the word] has two senses, like הוא עשנו ולא אנחנו (Psalms 100:3) — one sense: that we did not make ourselves; and the second: that we are his. But the correct view in my eyes is that this second alone is the truth, and all of them likewise. Rabbi Judah the Grammarian said: we cannot distinguish in pronunciation between לא with alef and לו with vav or heh, like הלה היא רבת בני עמון (Deuteronomy 3:11). All these verses have alef on the inside and vav on the outside; all of them, according to their reading, is their meaning. And know that the word והפדה is of the transitive verbs, like והפדך (Deuteronomy 15:6), אשר פדה את נפשי (2 Samuel 4:9), כי פדיתים (Zechariah 10:8). And behold, והפדה is a verb transitive to two objects, like המצמיח חציר (Psalms 147:8), or like 'Reuben fed Simeon bread.' And behold, והפדה: he shall seek her redemption and receive it, whether she redeems herself or her father or one of her relatives redeems her. For if she is close to six years, they shall reckon how many years she served, and how much distance remains until the seventh [year], or until the time when she is in her own authority; and according to the reckoning shall be the redemption." "<b>לעם נכרי — to a foreign people.</b> We have explained it. And know that every people that is not Israel is called נכר, and it is not like זר, for זר is called one who is not of the family of the tribe. Now if we say that Israel were called Hebrews on account of Ever, and he was a servant of HaShem, then whoever is of his family and of his faith is called עברי. And if we say they were so called on account of Abraham, behold it is written: כי ביצחק יקרא לך זרע (Genesis 21:12), even though concerning Ishmael it is written כי זרעך הוא (ibid. 21:13) — the land was not given except to Isaac alone. And the sons of Isaac were Jacob and Esau, and concerning Isaac it is written: כי לך ולזרעך אתן את כל הארצות האל (ibid. 26:3). And behold, he was not called 'seed' except in Jacob alone, to whom the land was given. And behold, the children of the concubines and the children of Esau with them are considered נכרים."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:58.815432974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}